{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786659530563308001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"algebraic-illstarred-mollusk","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"550593aa31b4ec477eaede30c7691c43b3a7fa1d4009646e352edd81223fec05","event_uuid":"1a129572-4d1d-473d-bcfd-400939a8dafd","position":{"commit_sha":"2369615e6dedcd2bd43ea2e19c739b9c03bdc670","position":"1786160096505602001-1a129572-4d1d-473d-bcfd-400939a8dafd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"202360b07739fc69a8310eafef578f1c9a840774de0fc83f8787ec9b505f36d5","event_uuid":"5f2cde70-f928-40c4-986d-9e56de6f403b","position":{"commit_sha":"e81d5044b7c3196b068f8f4d7b39b05d739af3de","position":"1786160170400258001-5f2cde70-f928-40c4-986d-9e56de6f403b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fffcc37baa42a8202ed93599c0022b5db8d1744fd684171200add7145437131f","event_uuid":"aee2eae7-4470-4bd7-b2ff-32dd455203db","position":{"commit_sha":"7b41839a8a69bb3f01f4c6df12c350ed044e233d","position":"1786160204546438001-aee2eae7-4470-4bd7-b2ff-32dd455203db"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e0d77e8605c24a8cb315a55ff0a9c726a6841cf94327e9a283b6d4e976890215","event_uuid":"a0de0e64-258b-4de7-9566-938a57cd019d","position":{"commit_sha":"a6902ed44e4b2e7c068e6b9246e65cee18b40b69","position":"1786162257829169001-a0de0e64-258b-4de7-9566-938a57cd019d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786160096505602001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"aee2eae7-4470-4bd7-b2ff-32dd455203db","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"},{"link_uuid":"a0de0e64-258b-4de7-9566-938a57cd019d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a33c-9001-9d86-4e59"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe inbound fetcher can only see one tracker project. `jqls_for(project)` builds exactly one pair of\nqueries — active and recent-done — from a single key\n(`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py:78-90`), and `_validate_project_key` refuses an empty\nor malformed key outright rather than searching unscoped (`fetcher.py:63-75`, bug `626d`). A store\nthat lists several projects in its mapping still ingests only one of them.\n\n## Approach\n\nFan out: call the existing `jqls_for` once per project in the store mapping and union the results\ninto the snapshot, rather than building a single `project IN (A,B)` query. Two concrete reasons.\nFirst, the per-query truncation ceiling (`_ACLI_CEILING = 1200` at `fetcher.py:91`, raising\n`SilentTruncationError`) stays scoped per project instead of becoming a shared budget that a single\nbusy project could exhaust on behalf of the others. Second, it reuses `jqls_for` and\n`_validate_project_key` unchanged, so the JQL-injection guard that bug `626d` added keeps applying to\nevery key with no new interpolation site.\n\nInbound-created tickets record their source project in `bridge_project` and get their `repos`\ndefaulted from that project's mapping entry. The existing local-id derivation already encodes the\nproject (`_jira_key_to_local_id`, `inbound_translate.py:120-124`, `DIG-123` → `jira-dig-123`), so ids\nstay unique across projects with no change; this story makes the association explicit on the ticket\nrather than only implicit in the id.\n\nThe CREATE event for an inbound ticket is written directly rather than through `create_core`\n(`apply_inbound_records.py:150-222`, which stamps `creation_channel` at `:221`), so the two new\nfields are stamped at that same site.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py`\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py`\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py`\n- tests under `tests/`\n\n## Testing\n\nTier per the shared standard's external-service row: a stateful verified fake fed production-shaped\nJira fixtures. The fake must record the queries issued, because \"one JQL pair per project\" is itself\nthe contract under test and is invisible to a result-only assertion.\n\n- Happy path: a mapping with two projects issues exactly two query pairs — one per key — and the\n  resulting snapshot contains issues from both.\n- Postcondition: each ticket created from the fetch records the project its issue came from, and its\n  `repos` equal that project's mapping entry.\n- Edge: a project listed in the mapping that returns zero issues contributes nothing and does not\n  fail the pass.\n- Failure path: one project exceeding the per-query ceiling raises `SilentTruncationError` naming\n  that project, and the ceiling is evaluated per project — a second project under the limit is not\n  penalised by the first. This is the contrast case that proves the budget is not shared.\n- Collateral invariant: a store whose mapping holds exactly one project issues the same query pair as\n  before this change, so single-project behaviour is untouched.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A mapping with two projects issues one JQL pair per project in a single pass; checked by a fake\n      transport recording the issued queries and asserting the exact pair count and contents.\n- [ ] Each inbound-created ticket records its source project and the repos from that project's\n      mapping entry; checked by asserting both fields on tickets created from a two-project fixture.\n- [ ] The truncation ceiling applies per project, not as a shared budget; checked by a test where one\n      project exceeds it and a second under-limit project still ingests successfully.\n- [ ] A single-project mapping issues an identical query pair to the pre-change behaviour; checked by\n      a regression test comparing the recorded queries.\n- [ ] A configured project returning zero issues does not fail the pass; checked by an empty-result\n      fixture.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"fan out jqls_for per configured project and union the snapshot"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py","reason":"stamp source project and defaulted repos on the inbound CREATE"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py","reason":"carry the source project through inbound translation"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","reason":"per-project query pair, per-project ceiling, single-project regression"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","a33c-9001-9d86-4e59"],["depends_on","cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"],["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1734-7c6d-5a6a-48fd","ticket_type":"story","title":"Multi-project inbound fetch: per-project JQL fan-out and source-project recording","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1a129572-4d1d-473d-bcfd-400939a8dafd","5f2cde70-f928-40c4-986d-9e56de6f403b","aee2eae7-4470-4bd7-b2ff-32dd455203db","a0de0e64-258b-4de7-9566-938a57cd019d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659530563308001,"uuid":"c925a618-cfc5-4b1d-a1ae-8ab2fd3b1d1a"}